rightkit-overlay-win: provenance of lifted and adapted work

This crate was written for Right Suite from two Orthic Labs sources. Neither is a third-party
work; the notices record where the techniques came from.

1. Pulse for Windows, `windows/src/canvas.rs` and `windows/src/surface.rs` (Orthic Labs, in the
   Pulse repository). The software rasteriser follows that canvas: premultiplied 0xAARRGGBB
   composition, signed-distance rounded rectangles, the clockwise ring-arc stroke with round caps,
   the sub-scanline polygon fill with exact horizontal coverage, the distance-field polyline
   stroke, and the top-down 32-bit DIB section presented with `UpdateLayeredWindow` and
   `AC_SRC_ALPHA`. The GDI grey-coverage text mask approach is from `surface.rs`. The continuous
   (squircle) corner (`Continuous`: Apple's three cubic Beziers per corner, a curve lookup table
   and sub-sampled edge coverage) and the bilinear premultiplied image blit (`draw_image`) from
   `canvas.rs` are carried over as `PaintCtx::fill_squircle`, `stroke_squircle`, `blit_rgba` and
   `blit_premultiplied`.

2. HeardRight native pill renderer, `tauri-app-next/src-tauri/src/pill_native.rs` as of commit
   a1361a06^ (Orthic Labs, in the HeardRight repository). The layered-window owner thread, the
   WM_MOUSELEAVE hover subscription, press/release click matching, the box-blur glass layer
   cache and the SVG path-data icon parser (arc-to-cubic conversion) come from it, re-expressed
   without tiny-skia or ab_glyph.

